ashington's departed dave raise your  hand here  dave is also part of the mac committee  it's wonderful to have these type  resources  and the wide range and diversity of  people that we have so this does  conclude this was an mac  press conference with the sheriff's  support and all the mac and we have  probably another 20 plus members who we  didn't invite to this but we wanted you  to  hear from the people who are directly  involved we've launched two new  subcommittees  one on recruiting one on mental health  and homelessness and one on reductions  of violence so  this mma committee is taking a stronger  role  in terms of the policy developments that  have been very effective with this  department and is excellent having the  relationship with the sheriff  and his executive command the mmac  commitments are available for you  after the press conference is over and  this brings it to a conclusion  thank all of you for coming out thank  the mac committee  and the yeah bringing attention to  everybody that point dura legrand who's  also just a very  excellent resource for us all and uh as  you all know carla  alston is leaving us now but we're in  very capable hands and carla let's  give carl a round of applause she's been  such an excellent resource  she's retiring the sheriff says that  she's independently wealthy i think she  received a major inheritance from  someone in her family so  she's going to say bon voyage too but  thank her and the good work that she's  done here  we can keep building on this so this  concludes the press conference again  thank all of you  and you have access to with all the mac  members again raise your hand  so you have access to them and let me  thank the eagles christian  uh family center and the youth  empowerment for summerlin for coming out  and being a part of this press  conference you are not the future you  are the now  and with metro is truth trust and  transparency  this department does it well the  community's involved thank you all very  much
 

